    "text": "US 9,551,933 B2\n231\n232\n-continued\n-continued\n(D-55)\n(D-62)\no\n5\nHO\nN\n(D-56)\n10\n(D-63)\nHO.\n15\nO\nN\n(D-57) 20\n(D-64)\n25\nN\n(D-58)\n30\n(D-65)\nN\nN\n35\nThe compound represented by formula (A) can be syn-\n40\nthesized by referring to, for example, JP-A-2007-298569\n(D-59)\nand JP-A-2009-199021.\nIn the present invention, as for the low molecular weight\nOH\ncompound (D), one compound may be used alone, or two or\nmore compounds may be mixed and used.\nH\n45\nThe composition of the present invention may or may not\ncontain the low molecular compound (D), but in the case of\n(D-60)\ncontaining the compound (D), the content thereof is usually\nfrom 0.001 to 20 mass %, preferably from 0.001 to 10 mass\n%, more preferably from 0.01 to 5 mass %, based on the total\n50\nsolid content of the composition combined with the basic\nN\ncompound.\nHO\nIn the case where the composition of the present invention\ncontains an acid generator, the ratio between the acid gen-\n(D-61)\nerator and the compound (D) used in the composition is\n55\n(by mol)=from 2.5 to 300. That is, the molar ratio is\npreferably acid generator/[compound (D)+basic compound]\npreferably 2.5 or more in view of sensitivity and resolution\nand is preferably 300 or less from the standpoint of sup-\nO\npressing the reduction in resolution due to thickening of the\nresist pattern over time after exposure until heat treatment.\nN\n60\nThe acid generator/[compound (D)+basic compound] (by\nmol) is more preferably from 5.0 to 200, still more prefer-\nably from 7.0 to 150.\nÖther examples of the basic compound which can be used\nin the composition of the present invention include com-\n65\npounds synthesized in Examples of JP-A-2002-363146 and\ncompounds described in paragraph 0108 of JP-A-2007-\n298569.",
